# bolthr: two decode-step headroom cuts on Nemotron 3.5 Bolt, every output bit as before. Base: 38f2c346a (this
# tree's parent), built in a detached worktree; the head is this tree.
# Resource timeline [per decode token]: host CPU one graph launch, PCIe the token in and the id out, host DRAM
# and NVMe nothing (the whole model sits on the card): none of them changes. The wall is the card's serial
# chain of nodes. Bytes 3.0 GB at ~700 GB/s explain 4.3 ms of the 11.3-11.4 ms step (3090 d=512 / A6000
# README row 87.5 tok/s); the rest is latency in short dependent nodes, which is where both cuts act. The
# step is not byte-bound, so a term shortened here is on the critical path, not under a shadow.
# H1 (mamba2_step norm tail, 40 Mamba-2 layers; 128 heads x 64, groups 8 [n_groups is not in the repo: the
# Super-family value, scales the term linearly], so per = 16, chunks = 4, bpg = 64 partials, width 1024).
# After the group's last ticket, thread 0 now sums the 64 f64 partials and the scale, one barrier hands it to
# the block (inside the ticket's thread-0 branch, so no new barrier); before, all 128 threads ran the sum.
# SASS [counted, ptxas 13.3 sm_86, `just sass-scan gate_nemotron_h_moe_e2e -- --exact mamba2_step`, base and
# head alike]: the sum is a 16-way unrolled volatile loop, 16 LDG.STRONG.SYS in flight, then 16 chained DADD;
# bpg 64 = 4 trips. Lanes 1..31 of warp 0 cost nothing (one warp instruction).
# Warps 1..3 run the same chain in parallel on their own schedulers, so they cost only where they share a
# resource: the FP64 pipe (GA102 1/64 rate, 2 lanes an SM [assumed: shared or per-partition is not
# settled by the SASS]). Shared pipe, 16 clk a warp DADD: 4 warps x 64 x 16 = 4096 clk against 1024 for one
# warp, 3072 clk = 1.8 us a layer at 1.7 GHz, x 40 = 72 us = 0.63 % of 11.4 ms. Per-partition pipe: the warps
# do not contend and thread 0 alone is 0. The shared word adds ~0.01 us a layer (no barrier is added: the
# ticket's own barrier carries it). H1 = 0..72 us [derived]; the status table's 88 us priced all four warps'
# adds and the one remaining warp at 0, which a warp instruction with one active lane does not get.
# H2 (flash_gqa seg_packs, 8 attention layers): the 4 segment launches a layer (2 key heads x 2 packs of 8
# query heads, one block grid of 80 each) are one launch of 4 x 80 blocks through a `packs` argument of the
# existing gqa_flash_seg / gqa_flash_seg_mma; the merge stays: 5 -> 2 nodes a layer, 24 nodes a step. The
# launch term alone is 24 x 0.85 us = 20 us (0.18 %). The nodes are a serial chain and each one runs only its
# live blocks (8 of 80 at d=512, 64 of 80 at d=4096, one per SM), so a node costs its block time, not the
# launch: 3 x (c_node + T_seg) a layer is removed, the merged launch's 4x blocks fit one wave of the 82-84 SMs
# (3-4 blocks an SM). T_seg is the one term the derivation cannot fix: 2..5 us [the h1grid card's 3-5 us
# for a 4-8 live block node is derived there, not measured; 2 us is the floor of one tile's staging and fold].
# 3 x (0.85 + 2..5) x 8 = 68..140 us = 0.60..1.23 %.
# Combined [derived]: step -68..-212 us of 11,400 us = +0.60..+1.9 % tok/s. The two cannot be told apart by this
# A/B, and H1 alone (0..0.63 %) sits inside the ruler at any round count: decide-below reads the nodes.
kind: ab
question: does one segment launch per attention layer plus a thread-0 norm scale in the Mamba-2 step shorten
  the Bolt decode step on the card?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96, depth 512, RTX A6000, Nemotron 3.5 Bolt (nemotron_h_moe) whole on one card — (head -
  base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +0.6..+1.9
rounds: 10
condition: one lease, BLOOMERY_TIMING_GPU = the A6000, both arms generate_qwen3moe (BLOOMERY_MODEL=nemotron_h_moe
  BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=10 just depth-gpu-qwen3moe 512 bin:<base tree>/target/release/generate_qwen3moe:512), the
  base built from 38f2c346a in its own remote dir, the arm order rotated every round; the witness block clean
  at start and end (no [cpu-busy], no [other-busy], card clocks printed); the head's gate-gpu-nemotron-h-moe-e2e
  structure line green on its round ledger (group8_segments = attn layers, graph nodes 24 fewer than the
  base's at 8 attention layers); depth 4096 read in the same lease as a second pair, not as the term
decide-in: +0.6..+1.9 %: land both as derived and record T_seg and the FP64 pipe term in rig-log from the
  interval and the node count
decide-below: under +0.6 %: if the paired interval excludes 0 land (smaller than derived) and take one nsys step
  of each binary for the gqa_flash_seg_mma and mamba2_step node times (T_seg under 2 us, or the FP64 pipe is
  per-partition); if it includes 0, read the head's nodes in that nsys before any further lever
decide-above: above +1.9 %: more of the serial chain sat in these nodes than derived: open the norm tail's
  elementwise loop (8 trips of two dependent loads) and the partial preload next, from the same nsys
